WEBVTT

1
00:00:09.067 --> 00:00:11.715
Sally: Dr. Smith, what is this?

2
00:00:11.716 --> 00:00:14.194
Dr. Smith: That is a time machine, Sally.

3
00:00:14.195 --> 00:00:17.686
Dr. Smith: With this machine, we can go back in time.

4
00:00:17.687 --> 00:00:21.194
Sally and Tim: Wow! Can we try it?

5
00:00:21.195 --> 00:00:24.788
Dr. Smith: Of course! Where do you want to go?

6
00:00:24.789 --> 00:00:27.473
Tim: I want to see the dinosaurs.

7
00:00:27.474 --> 00:00:30.273
Dr. Smith: No problem. Let's go!

8
00:00:30.274 --> 00:00:34.113
Dr. Smith: Hop in, Tim! Hop in, Sally!

9
00:00:34.114 --> 00:00:38.383
Dr. Smith: Here we are, 65 million years ago.

10
00:00:38.384 --> 00:00:41.768
Sally: Wow! It looks very different.

11
00:00:41.769 --> 00:00:44.221
Everything is so big.

12
00:00:44.222 --> 00:00:47.927
Dr. Smith: Yes, many of the plants are very big.

13
00:00:47.928 --> 00:00:52.004
Tim: Dr. Smith, I don't see the dinosaurs.

14
00:00:52.005 --> 00:00:54.110
Dr. Smith: Look up.

15
00:00:54.111 --> 00:00:58.242
Tim: Wow! It's huge and scary-looking.

16
00:00:58.243 --> 00:01:00.116
Will it eat me?

17
00:01:00.117 --> 00:01:02.385
Dr. Smith: No, it won't eat you, Tim.

18
00:01:02.386 --> 00:01:04.606
It is a plant eater.

19
00:01:04.607 --> 00:01:07.784
Tim: Whew! That's good.

20
00:01:07.785 --> 00:01:10.338
Dr. Smith: Besides, it's only a baby.

21
00:01:10.339 --> 00:01:13.873
Look over there, that is its mother.

22
00:01:13.874 --> 00:01:15.923
Sally and Tim: Wow!

23
00:01:15.924 --> 00:01:19.705
Sally: That dinosaur sure is big.

24
00:01:19.706 --> 00:01:23.829
Dr. Smith: That is one of the biggest dinosaurs ever, Sally.

25
00:01:23.830 --> 00:01:26.363
Dr. Smith: It is called a Brontosaurus.

26
00:01:26.364 --> 00:01:32.605
Dr. Smith: It weighs more than 28 tons and is about 25 meters long.

27
00:01:32.606 --> 00:01:35.313
Tim: I hope it doesn't step on me.

28
00:01:35.314 --> 00:01:38.188
Dr. Smith: That would be very bad.

29
00:01:38.189 --> 00:01:41.717
Let's explore more! But be careful.

30
00:01:41.718 --> 00:01:44.054
Sally: Look at that dinosaur.

31
00:01:44.055 --> 00:01:47.060
It is smaller than the other ones.

32
00:01:47.061 --> 00:01:49.571
Dr. Smith: Yes, it is an Iguanodon.

33
00:01:49.572 --> 00:01:51.839
It's a plant eater too.

34
00:01:51.840 --> 00:01:55.729
Tim: If it's a plant eater, it won't hurt me.

35
00:01:55.730 --> 00:01:59.627
Tim: Hello, Iguanodon. How are you today?

36
00:01:59.628 --> 00:02:02.222
Dr. Smith: Tim, watch out!

37
00:02:02.223 --> 00:02:04.768
Sally: That was close.

38
00:02:04.769 --> 00:02:08.000
It almost hit you with its tail.

39
00:02:08.001 --> 00:02:11.960
Dr. Smith: Yes, the Iguanodon has a very powerful tail.

40
00:02:11.961 --> 00:02:15.129
Dr. Smith: It can use its tail when it is attacked.

41
00:02:15.130 --> 00:02:19.156
Sally: It also uses it to hit small boys.

42
00:02:19.157 --> 00:02:21.388
All: Ha-ha-ha!

43
00:02:21.389 --> 00:02:24.060
Tim: Maybe we should leave it alone.

44
00:02:24.061 --> 00:02:26.903
Dr. Smith: That's a good idea, Tim.

45
00:02:26.904 --> 00:02:29.223
Sally: Ah! Look over there.

46
00:02:29.224 --> 00:02:31.280
Look at that dinosaur.

47
00:02:31.281 --> 00:02:34.401
Sally: It has a very large head.

48
00:02:34.402 --> 00:02:36.801
What's its name, Dr. Smith?

49
00:02:36.802 --> 00:02:39.099
Dr. Smith: It's a Triceratops.

50
00:02:39.100 --> 00:02:43.192
Its head is very big and it has three horns.

51
00:02:43.193 --> 00:02:46.342
Tim: Its horns look very sharp.

52
00:02:46.343 --> 00:02:47.959
Dr. Smith: Yes, they are.

53
00:02:47.960 --> 00:02:52.834
Dr. Smith: You can see one horn on its nose and the other two above its eyes.

54
00:02:52.835 --> 00:02:56.426
Dr. Smith: It uses the horns to protect itself.

55
00:02:56.427 --> 00:02:59.248
Tim: I hope it doesn't poke me.

56
00:02:59.249 --> 00:03:02.420
Sally: There's a very interesting dinosaur.

57
00:03:02.421 --> 00:03:07.088
Sally: It's very big, but it has a very small mouth.

58
00:03:07.089 --> 00:03:09.494
I wonder how it eats.

59
00:03:09.495 --> 00:03:11.649
Dr. Smith: That is a Stegosaurus.

60
00:03:11.650 --> 00:03:13.766
It's a plant eater too.

61
00:03:13.767 --> 00:03:18.267
Dr. Smith: You're right. It does have a very small mouth.

62
00:03:18.268 --> 00:03:21.872
Tim: Look at its back. It's bumpy.

63
00:03:21.873 --> 00:03:24.685
Dr. Smith: Those are called back plates, Tim.

64
00:03:24.686 --> 00:03:27.804
Dr. Smith: The Stegosaurus uses them for protection.

65
00:03:27.805 --> 00:03:34.352
Sally: Dr. Smith, I think that all plant eaters [n3@have some way to protect themselves.

66
00:03:34.353 --> 00:03:37.024
Dr. Smith: Yes, Sally, you're right.

67
00:03:37.025 --> 00:03:40.167
Tim: Look over there. What's that?

68
00:03:40.168 --> 00:03:43.760
Sally: It looks like a giant egg.

69
00:03:43.761 --> 00:03:45.238
Dr. Smith: Oh, don't touch it.

70
00:03:45.239 --> 00:03:47.083
It's a dinosaur egg.

71
00:03:47.084 --> 00:03:50.340
Dr. Smith: Soon, a baby dinosaur will hatch from it.

72
00:03:50.341 --> 00:03:54.781
Sally: Really? Do all dinosaurs hatch from eggs?

73
00:03:54.782 --> 00:03:58.634
Dr. Smith: Yes, they do.

74
00:03:58.635 --> 00:04:02.005
Oh my! Did you hear that roar?

75
00:04:02.006 --> 00:04:05.147
Tim: Why are the animals running away?

76
00:04:05.148 --> 00:04:07.620
They look very scared.

77
00:04:07.621 --> 00:04:10.360
Dr. Smith: That is a Tyrannosaurus.

78
00:04:10.361 --> 00:04:13.125
Tim: It looks dangerous.

79
00:04:13.126 --> 00:04:15.562
Dr. Smith: It is. It's a meat eater.

80
00:04:15.563 --> 00:04:17.663
Tim: What does that mean?

81
00:04:17.664 --> 00:04:20.021
Sally: It means we should run.

82
00:04:20.022 --> 00:04:23.379
Dr. Smith: That's right! Run, Tim! Run, Sally!

83
00:04:23.380 --> 00:04:25.595
Let's get out of here.

84
00:04:25.596 --> 00:04:28.248
Dr. Smith: Here's the time machine. Hop in!

85
00:04:28.249 --> 00:04:30.621
Come on, we have to be quick.

86
00:04:30.622 --> 00:04:34.356
Sally: Oh no! Here comes the Tyrannosaurus.

87
00:04:34.357 --> 00:04:37.470
Tim: Hurry, hurry, hurry!

88
00:04:37.471 --> 00:04:41.281
Dr. Smith: Now, where is the "present" button?

89
00:04:41.282 --> 00:04:43.166
Sally: Hurry!

90
00:04:43.167 --> 00:04:45.480
Dr. Smith: I found it. Whew!

91
00:04:45.481 --> 00:04:49.532
Dr. Smith: Soon we will be back in the present, safe and sound.

92
00:04:49.533 --> 00:04:55.299
Tim: That was fun!

93
00:04:55.300 --> 00:04:59.488
Dr. Smith, what happened to the dinosaurs?

94
00:04:59.489 --> 00:05:02.243
Dr. Smith: They became extinct, Tim.

95
00:05:02.244 --> 00:05:05.589
Sally: Really! How did that happen?

96
00:05:05.590 --> 00:05:09.392
Dr. Smith: Some people think that a very large rock crashed into Earth.

97
00:05:09.393 --> 00:05:13.803
Dr. Smith: There was a lot of smoke and dust, and then the sun went away.

98
00:05:13.804 --> 00:05:18.036
Tim: Without the sun, all the dinosaurs died?

99
00:05:18.037 --> 00:05:20.177
Dr. Smith: Right.

100
00:05:20.178 --> 00:05:22.966
Sally: Dr. Smith, we have to go.

101
00:05:22.967 --> 00:05:26.049
Our mother said to be home by five.

102
00:05:26.050 --> 00:05:28.394
Dr. Smith: You had better go quickly.

103
00:05:28.395 --> 00:05:31.480
Tim: Thank you, Dr. Smith. Good-bye!

104
00:05:31.481 --> 00:05:33.365
Dr. Smith: Good-bye.
